+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -uo pipefail
+
+if [[ "$#" -lt 2 ]]; then
+  printf 'usage: %s LOGFILE COMMAND [ARG ...]\n' "$0" >&2
+  exit 64
+fi
+
+audit_log=$1
+shift
+
+{
+  printf 'WORKDIR: %q\n' "$PWD"
+  printf 'COMMAND:'
+  printf ' %q' "$@"
+  printf '\n'
+  "$@"
+  audit_status=$?
+  printf 'EXIT_STATUS: %d\n' "$audit_status"
+  exit "$audit_status"
+} 2>&1 | tee "$audit_log"
+
+exit "${PIPESTATUS[0]}"

The detailed seven-stage review, trust ledger, exhaustive rule inventory, scripts, mutations, and bounded logs are complete and internally validated.
  ✓ Read required Kit skills and verify audit infrastructure/provenance integrity
  ✓ Check source fidelity and run independent Python differential tests
  ✓ Rebuild semantics/proof definitions and execute all positive claims
  ✓ Audit claim adequacy, real-program pinning, and concrete witnesses
  ✓ Inventory and review every K declaration and rule for soundness
  ✓ Create and run a fresh meaningful non-vacuity mutation
  ✓ Account for proven versus assumed boundaries and write REVIEW.md
